__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
.env
target/
node_modules/
.claude/
.pytest_cache/
.anchor/
test-ledger/

# The evidence SQLite store is the working store, not the committed artifact
# (D-04). What is committed is the deterministic text export in
# state/evidence/*.jsonl, which this pattern does not match.
state/*.db
state/*.db-wal
state/*.db-shm

# Planning artifacts live in the working repo, not in the published one.
.planning/

# Agent tooling configuration, not project documentation. Nothing a verifier
# needs, and it is the clearest authorship tell in the tree.
CLAUDE.md

# The append-only observation log is the local working record. It carries
# superseded schema-1 rows whose wording predates the current spec, and the
# committed public evidence is state/evidence/*.jsonl plus the record
# published beside each coin page -- both regenerated from the current code.
state/observations.jsonl
marketing/video/scaffold.mov
marketing/video/*.mov
marketing/video/renders/
marketing/video/masters/
marketing/video/manim/media/
marketing/video/capture/_rec/
marketing/video/capture/*.webm
marketing/video/capture/*.mp4
marketing/video/capture/*.mov

# The video campaign's working tree. Its renders, clips and scaffold footage
# were already ignored by the patterns above; the scripts and runbooks beside
# them are working material for that campaign rather than part of the
# protocol, and nothing in the repository imports or runs them. Kept on disk,
# out of the repository. Kept in the operator's own backup, not here:
# these paths were purged from history rather than merely untracked.
marketing/

# Ops-only, not part of the published protocol.
#
# posts/ is the unposted half of building in public: X drafts written down
# before they go out, with the register, the targets and the sequencing
# beside them. The posted version is public the moment it is posted; the
# draft and the reasoning behind it are not.
posts/

# Scratch inputs from measuring coins by hand. No code or test reads any of
# them (checked by literal filename). Each datum is public on chain, but the
# curated list is an ops signal: it says which coins were being scanned and
# when.
_cfgs.txt
_mints.txt
_enrollable.json

# The internal handoff. Names the funded fee-payer wallet and its balance,
# which secrets are set in which repository, and the open-items roadmap.
# Operational detail about running the protocol, not about verifying it --
# and the wallet it names pays for every crank run.
HANDOFF.md

# Keypairs, anywhere. Both repositories are public, and a Solana keypair is
# an ordinary-looking JSON array of 64 integers -- nothing about the file
# announces what it is, so the pattern is here rather than relying on
# noticing. HANDOFF.md: keys are the owner's to generate and rotate, and a
# key that reaches a commit is burned whatever its balance was.
*keypair*.json
keeper.json
id.json
